--- A. REJECTION-SAMPLING DISTRIBUTION (2000 signing calls each;
       attempts read directly from base_attempts / las_attempts) ---
   operation                   avg accept%   min   max   p50   p95
   Base Sign (no t')         2.720   36.8%     1    15     2     7
   LAS PreSign (folds t')    2.727   36.7%     1    18     2     7
   avg = mean attempts/sig; accept% = 1/avg; both schemes reject under
   Fiat-Shamir-with-aborts at the bound gamma-kappa (Base Sign) /
   gamma-kappa-1 (LAS PreSign).
   Run-validity gates below cover the 5 x 500 TIMED sign-class calls of EACH
   tier of the primary table -- the packed sign-class calls wrap the same
   rejection loop -- (same 5-sigma check and line format as the Rust drivers):
rejection gate [Algorithm 1 Sign]: 2500 calls, measured 2.6332 attempts/call (acceptance 37.98%) vs theory 2.7186 (36.78%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.2162 => OK
rejection gate [Algorithm 2 PreSign]: 2500 calls, measured 2.8360 attempts/call (acceptance 35.26%) vs theory 2.7643 (36.18%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.2208 => OK
rejection gate [Algorithm 1 Sign (packed tier)]: 2500 calls, measured 2.6900 attempts/call (acceptance 37.17%) vs theory 2.7186 (36.78%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.2162 => OK
rejection gate [Algorithm 2 PreSign (packed tier)]: 2500 calls, measured 2.7108 attempts/call (acceptance 36.89%) vs theory 2.7643 (36.18%), 5-sigma tolerance +-0.2208 => OK
per-attempt diagnostic (rejection-normalised): Sign 376.6 +/- 12.2 us | PreSign 369.9 +/- 5.4 us | overhead -1.8%

--- B. ADAPT TIMING CLARIFICATION (microseconds, mean +/- SD) ---
   Adapt checked total       289.955 +/-  8.442   (PROTOCOL: las_adapt above, incl. internal PreVerify)
   witness-add only            8.441 +/-  0.168   (DIAGNOSTIC ONLY: z=z_hat+r'; not a protocol op)
   A real Adapt MUST pre-verify first; the witness-add line is a lower bound,
   not a usable operation.  Use 'Adapt checked total' for protocol cost.

--- C. COMMUNICATION (packed bytes; BYTE-LEVEL only, NOT EVM gas) ---
   public key    pk = t                5888
   secret key    sk = r                 960
   statement     Y = t'               5888   (64.3% of the signature; t' has pk size)
   witness       r'                    960   (same packed layout as sk = r)
   challenge     c_tilde                32   (32-byte H digest)
   response      z (final)            9120   (99.7% of the signature)
   response      z_hat (pre-sig)      9120   (same packed layout as z)
   signature         (c, z)           9152
   pre-signature     (c, z_hat)       9152   (same size as the signature)
   final adapted sig (c, z)           9152   (an ordinary signature)
   commitment    w = A*y            internal computed commitment; hashed into c; not transmitted
   -- protocol-component catalogue (context; what each object is / why counted or not) --
   pp=(A,H)  A' seed                    32   (public params; only this 32-byte seed is transmitted)
   pp=(A,H)  expanded A'             41216   (n*ell polys; DERIVED from the seed, NOT transmitted)
   y (signing mask, S_gamma)         9120   (n+ell polys; INTERNAL, hashed into c via w, NOT transmitted)
   w = A*y (commitment)              5888   (n polys; INTERNAL, hashed into c, NOT transmitted)
   pi (NIZK well-formedness proof)    n/a   (paper-level off-chain proof; NOT implemented / NOT measured)
   tx metadata (addrs/amounts/nonces) excl   (application/ledger layer; EXCLUDED from this accounting)
   atomic-swap payload (byte-level only):
     off-chain   = Y + 2*pre-signature        =  24192   [= t' + 2*(c, z_hat)]
     settlement  = 2*signature                =  18304   [= 2*(c, z)]
     settlement incl. escrowed Y = Y + 2*sig  =  24192
   (EVM/keccak gas for on-chain verification is a separate axis; see evm/.)

--- D. COMPONENT MICROBENCHMARKS (microseconds, mean +/- SD) ---
   Cost-attribution ESTIMATES timing LOCAL COPIES of the inner steps
   (behaviourally identical to las.c) -- NOT the protocol entry points above.
   A-product / commitment w = A*y                         99.504 +/-  5.569
   challenge hash  c = H(pk, w(+t'), M)                  104.943 +/- 16.532
   NTT(s)  (n+ell polys; ONCE PER CALL, hoisted)          46.307 +/-  1.265
   NTT(c)  (one poly; once per attempt / per verify)       2.928 +/-  0.181
   c*r  (one poly; pointwise+invNTT, operands pre-NTT'd)   5.015 +/-  0.674
   c*r  per attempt (NTT(c) + n+ell pointwise+invNTT)     72.731 +/-  1.264
   norm check  |z|inf over n+ell polys                     3.650 +/-  0.041
   w + t'   (n polys)                                      8.661 +/-  0.057
   z_hat + witness r'   (n+ell polys)                      8.441 +/-  0.168
   c*t  per verify (NTT(c) + n x (NTT(t)+pw+invNTT))      64.579 +/-  2.180
   KeyGen/Gen: sample r (n+ell ternary polys)             13.507 +/-  0.788
     (KeyGen = sample r + A*r; A*r is the A-product line above; statement Y gen = KeyGen)
   Ext: s = z - z_hat   (n+ell polys)                      9.242 +/-  0.372
   Ext: A*s   (recompute statement; = an A-product)      101.763 +/-  4.268
   Ext: t' == A*s check   (n polys)                        1.638 +/-  0.171
   note: a full Sign/PreSign attempt applies c*r across N_PLUS_ELL = n+ell = 15
         response polynomials; Verify-style challenge multiplication applies
         c*t across LAS_N = n = 8 public-key polynomials.  NTT hoisting
         follows upstream ref/sign.c: NTT(s) is paid once per CALL (amortised
         over ~e rejection attempts), NTT(c) once per attempt / per verify.

--- E. NORM-MARGIN DIAGNOSTICS (achieved infinity-norm vs the reject bound;
       max over the 2000 sampled accepted signatures from section A) ---
   accepted |z|inf      max    230340   vs accept limit g-k   =    230340   (100.00% of band)
   accepted |z^|inf     max    230339   vs accept limit g-k-1 =    230339   (100.00% of band)
   Interpretation: the RESPONSE z/z^ saturates its band (~100%) -- the bound is
   the binding constraint and is exactly why ~63% of attempts are rejected.
   Contrast the AMHL cumulative WITNESS ||s_j||inf, which is tiny (<=K) vs the
   g-k-K band: that bound is extremely loose (see bench_app, the K-series table).
